rule AvailabilityDefinition
	lineageTag: e8b78d4e-db69-554c-ab00-dc304b400085
	statement: Availability is measured as running samples divided by all machine-status samples, so Idle time (Starved or Blocked) lowers a machine's measured availability. The plant policy document defines Availability excluding Idle; reports and dashboards use the measured definition, and the station OEE escalation check (rule StationOeeEscalation) uses the policy's, because idle time counts against the station that caused it (rule StarvedBlockedRootCause).

	ruleReferencedEntity equipment#Machine
		propertyScope: specific
		ruleReferencedProperty is_running
		ruleReferencedProperty machine_status
